@startuml
title TMFC005 : Product Inventory -- eTOM/SID ABE Links

class "L2 - Product Inventory Management" as L2ProductInventoryManagement <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class "L2 - Loyalty Program Management/L3 - Loyalty Program Operation*" as L2LoyaltyProgramManagement <<eTOM Business Activity>>
class Product <<SID Data Entity>>
class "Loyalty**" as Loyalty <<SID Data Entity>>

' Per the image's own legend: an arrow from an eTOM activity towards a SID ABE
' means the information is produced by the activity; the arrow in the other
' direction means the information is consumed by the activity.
'
' Arrow directions below were confirmed by cropping and zooming into the
' arrowhead region of the source image (see full_box.png / top_junction.png /
' bottom_junction.png crops) rather than trusting a single full-image read --
' the Product pair genuinely has both directions drawn (a produced/consumed
' loop, as in TMFC039's own diagram), but the Loyalty pair does NOT: both of
' its arrows point INTO an eTOM activity box (both "is consumed by"), with no
' reverse "produces" arrow drawn from either activity into Loyalty. This
' asymmetry is real in the source, not an omission in the transcription.
L2ProductInventoryManagement --> Product : produces
Product --> L2ProductInventoryManagement : is consumed by

Loyalty --> L2ProductInventoryManagement : is consumed by
Loyalty --> L2LoyaltyProgramManagement : is consumed by

footer TMFC005 - Product Inventory (* partial ** for Loyalty Program, as printed in the source image)
@enduml
